+# ============================================
+# Raise kern.ipc.maxsockbuf for open5gs SCTP sockets
+# ============================================
+# open5gs' S1AP (mmed) and NGAP (amfd) interfaces open SCTP sockets. The
+# FreeBSD SCTP stack computes its default send/recv buffer size at boot from
+# the kernel's compiled-in SB_MAX constant, independent of the *live*
+# kern.ipc.maxsockbuf ceiling - on stock FreeBSD 14/15 those two numbers can
+# disagree, and when the default maxsockbuf ceiling ends up smaller than what
+# SCTP requests, socket() fails with ENOBUFS ("No buffer space available")
+# and the daemon aborts before it can bind its S1AP/NGAP listener. This is a
+# known FreeBSD/OPNsense base-tuning gap, not an open5gs bug - see e.g.
+# opnsense/plugins#5422, where FRR hit the identical symptom.
+#
+# kern.ipc.maxsockbuf has no loader-tunable hook (it can't be set via
+# /boot/loader.conf), so it has to go through OPNsense's own Tunables model
+# (System > Settings > Tunables / config.xml <sysctl>) rather than a raw
+# /etc/sysctl.conf edit, which OPNsense's config sync would otherwise
+# overwrite on the next boot or config apply.
